---

import AboutArticle from "../../components/AboutArticle.astro";
import { getAboutPage } from "../../lib/aboutPages";

const page = getAboutPage("esp32-ota-firmware")!;
---
<AboutArticle slug={page.slug} title={page.title} description={page.description}>
  <h2>OTA updates</h2>
  <p>
    Use the Arduino OTA or ESP-IDF HTTPS OTA libraries on your LAN, then POST readings to ThermalTrace
    over HTTPS. OTA and ingest are independent — firmware updates locally while telemetry uses
    <code>/api/ingest/&lt;key&gt;</code>.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`#include <ArduinoOTA.h>
// After WiFi.connect():
ArduinoOTA.begin();
// in loop():
ArduinoOTA.handle();`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Battery and RSSI in ingest</h2>
  <p>
    Include optional top-level fields so the Devices page and health alerts stay accurate:
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`{
  "temp1": 42.5,
  "door1": false,
  "battery": 87,
  "rssi": -62
}`}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Enable low-battery and weak-signal alerts under Dashboard → Alerts → Device health.
  </p>
</AboutArticle>
